&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Onsite Role - Office First&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the Platform tribe, we&#39;re building a self-service, AI-ready &lt;strong&gt;Data Platform&lt;/strong&gt; that powers SumUp&#39;s next big bets: data, AI, and real-time analytics. Our team designs and runs the infrastructure that lets data engineers, analysts, and ML teams across the business ship reliable pipelines and products without reinventing the wheel each time. This role sits at the centre of that work, giving you a genuine chance to shape how thousands of SumUppers build with data every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and evolve the data platform&#39;s infrastructure (Terraform, Kubernetes, GCP), so every environment is reproducible, version-controlled, and auditable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take end-to-end ownership of the reliability, performance, and scalability of the Data and AI platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop self-service features, including for ETL and orchestration, so teams can move faster without bespoke integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate operations to keep the platform highly available and cost-efficient as demand grows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate emerging technologies and shape adoption strategies that improve platform capabilities and business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product, infrastructure, data engineering, analytics, and AI/ML teams to make the standard path easier and safer than one-off integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;More than 4 years of experience building &lt;strong&gt;internal platforms&lt;/strong&gt; consumed by other teams, in a Data, Platform, or Software Engineering role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software engineering background in&lt;strong&gt; Python or Go&lt;/strong&gt;, along with solid SQL skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on knowledge of infrastructure and containerisation, such as&lt;strong&gt; Terraform,&lt;/strong&gt; Helm, Docker, and &lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with observability, monitoring, alerting, and platform reliability engineering practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in modern data stack (dbt, Snowflake, Trino, Airflow, etc.)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of setting up SDLC practices for analytics teams, including Git workflows, CI/CD, testing, and documentation standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;It&#39;s OK if you don&#39;t meet 100% of these criteria. If you&#39;re missing a few, it just means you&#39;ll have room to learn and grow with us.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real-time streaming experience (e.g. Kafka, Flink, StarRocks, Pinot, Druid, ClickHouse)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with systems at petabyte scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing AI-enabled systems, such as agentic SRE or AI automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 Opportunity to work with SumUppers globally on large-scale fintech products used by millions of businesses worldwide, from our Berlin office. This involves an office-first setup&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone&#39;s perspectives are respected and embraced&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚀 Enrolment onto our Virtual Stock Option programme: you will own a stake in SumUp&#39;s future success&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;amp;D budget of €2000 for your individual development, which can be used to attend conferenc

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Grafana Labs is the company behind Grafana Cloud, the fully managed observability platform trusted by more than 10,000 organizations to ensure reliability, resolve incidents faster, and optimize telemetry at scale. Built on open source and open standards and designed for interoperability across any stack, Grafana Cloud brings AI to observability and observability to AI, giving teams (and their agents) unified visibility so they can see, understand, and act on all their disparate data, wherever it lives, and move at the speed of their ambitions. Customers, including Anthropic, Bloomberg, NVIDIA, Microsoft, and Salesforce, rely on Grafana Labs. We are a 100% remote company with team members across 40+ countries, backed by leading investors including Lightspeed Venture Partners, Sequoia Capital, GIC, Coatue, J.P. Morgan, CapitalG, and Lead Edge Capital. Learn more at &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://grafana.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;grafana.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and follow us on &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/grafana-labs/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/grafana&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re scaling fast and staying true to what makes us different: an open-source legacy, a global collaborative culture, and a passion for meaningful work. Our team thrives in an innovation-driven environment where transparency, autonomy, and trust fuel everything we do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may not meet every requirement, and that’s okay. If this role excites you, we’d love you to raise your hand for what could be a truly career-defining opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a remote opportunity and we would be interested in applications from the UK, Ireland, Spain and Germany.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Grafana Cloud Observability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Grafana Cloud is our fully managed observability platform that integrates metrics, logs, and traces with Grafana. It allows our customers to use the best open source observability software, including Prometheus, Mimir, Loki, and Tempo, without the overhead of installing, maintaining and scaling their own observability stack.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within the Observability department, we build products that help customers understand and troubleshoot their applications and infrastructure. We work closely with product management, design and other engineering squads to provide seamless and highly curated experiences for our customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The squad: Database Observability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We build and evolve Grafana Cloud Database Observability. We want to help users understand the health and performance of their databases, identify slow queries and troubleshoot issues through clear, actionable insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a frontend engineer on the squad, you’ll build experiences that make complex database telemetry easy to explore and understand. You’ll work closely with backend engineers, product management and design to take ideas from early exploration through to production and improve them based on customer feedback.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our frontend stack is primarily TypeScript and React, interacting with backends written in Go. Your primary focus will be frontend engineering, with opportunities to work across the stack, contributing to APIs and backend functionality to deliver complete customer experiences. Frontend engineers at Grafana also have opportunities to contribute to open source communities.&lt;/p&gt;
